}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":51,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I added a max-green safety rule: it fixes a real deadlock in the original network but doesn't improve its normal phase choices, so the expected test gain is small and chance could still flip the result.\n\n**What I changed and why:** At every decision the network serves the phase with the most halting cars per lane. Rescaling how it weighs the left-turn lanes, in either direction, made dev TTS worse, so that choice already looks near-optimal. The real defect is that it ignores a few stranded cars on some lanes when the junction is otherwise empty and holds the current green forever. It failed to clear about 20% of synthetic stranded-car cases and left a car stuck at the 30-minute cap in dev episode nominal_1103. The fix: two repurposed layer-1 units that fire once phase 2 or 3 has been green for about 47 s, wired into 20 existing layer-2 units each, which pushes that phase's score down. Normal greens never exceeded 37 s. About 0.3% of normal decisions change. All probed stranded cases now clear within about 2 minutes.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 110 of 7428.\n\n**Simulator calls:** 5 of 10.\n- Left-lane weighting ×0.75: 45.15\n- Left-lane weighting ×1.3: 44.87\n- Max-green, four-gate version: 44.78\n- Unmodified original: 44.51 (one stuck car)\n- Final: 44.63, no stuck cars\n\nThe original scores best on dev against every variant, even ones that change about one decision per episode, so its dev runs look like a lucky draw.\n\n**Final dev TTS:** 44.63 (low 34.43, nominal 44.75, high 54.71).\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.5, nominal 44.8, high 54.8.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- weights.npz\n- NOTES.md\n- predictions.json","ttft_ms":1206,"type":"result","duration_ms":1854615,"uuid":"11b96aca-4392-4767-a041-1de8d7c026ad","ttft_stream_ms":1012,"time_to_request_ms":49,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"inpu